                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL",
                "headline": "Flood Warning issued September 14 at 9:25PM EDT by NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL",
                "description": "...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nWithlacoochee At US 41 Dunnellon affecting Marion, Citrus and Levy\nCounties.\n\n.Elevated water levels are expected along the river over the next\nseveral days due to recent heavy rainfall.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Withlacoochee at US 41 Dunnellon.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 28.2 feet, Docks and boat ramps flood along the river\nin Citrus and Marion counties.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:45 PM EDT Monday the stage was 28.2 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 28.2 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage just\nafter midnight tonight and continue rising to 28.2 feet just\nafter midnight tonight. Additional rises are possible thereafter.\n- Flood stage is 28.2 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 28.4\nfeet on 08/05/2024.\n- https://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Tuesday afternoon at 200 PM EDT.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
