                "headline": "Flood Warning issued September 14 at 9:23PM EDT by NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL",
                "description": "...The National Weather Service in Tampa Bay Ruskin has issued a\nFlood Warning for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nHorse Creek Near Arcadia at SR 72 affecting DeSoto County.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Horse Creek near Arcadia at SR 72.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday morning until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 12.0 feet, The access road to Hidden Oak is\nimpassable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:30 PM EDT Monday the stage was 9.3 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 12.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage late\nWednesday morning and continue rising to 12.4 feet Thursday\nevening. Additional rises are possible thereafter.\n- Flood stage is 12.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 12.5\nfeet on 08/31/2002.\n- https://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
